IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja1-part3-div5-6`

-- Tests for scja1-part3-div5-6.l4 (ss 23 to 28A). Expected values are written from the text (SCJA1969.txt lines 1885-2033), not from the code.

§§ `s 23: revision of criminal proceedings of subordinate courts`

-- inputs: the court, a written law gives a right of appeal from its decisions to the Supreme Court, the nature of the proceedings, the powers are exercised in accordance with the criminal procedure law
#ASSERT (`s 23 the General Division may exercise powers of revision in the criminal proceedings` `District Court` FALSE `a criminal proceeding` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 23 the General Division may exercise powers of revision in the criminal proceedings` `Magistrate's Court` FALSE `a criminal proceeding` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 23 the General Division may exercise powers of revision in the criminal proceedings` `Youth Court` FALSE `a criminal proceeding` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not in accordance with the criminal procedure law
#ASSERT (`s 23 the General Division may exercise powers of revision in the criminal proceedings` `District Court` FALSE `a criminal proceeding` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- civil proceedings are not "criminal proceedings and matters"
#ASSERT (`s 23 the General Division may exercise powers of revision in the criminal proceedings` `District Court` FALSE `a civil proceeding` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a tribunal that is a subordinate court only if a written law gives a right of appeal from it to the Supreme Court
#ASSERT (`s 23 the General Division may exercise powers of revision in the criminal proceedings` `another subordinate court, tribunal or judicial or quasi-judicial body` TRUE `a criminal proceeding` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 23 the General Division may exercise powers of revision in the criminal proceedings` `another subordinate court, tribunal or judicial or quasi-judicial body` FALSE `a criminal proceeding` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the Court of Appeal is not defined as a subordinate court
#ASSERT (`s 23 the General Division may exercise powers of revision in the criminal proceedings` `Court of Appeal` FALSE `a criminal proceeding` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 24 and 25: civil proceedings in subordinate courts`

-- s 24: inputs are the court, the appeal-right flag, the nature, the purpose
#ASSERT (`s 24 the General Division may call for and examine the record of the civil proceedings` `District Court` FALSE `a civil proceeding` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 24 the General Division may call for and examine the record of the civil proceedings` `Family Court` FALSE `a civil proceeding` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 24 the General Division may call for and examine the record of the civil proceedings` `District Court` FALSE `a civil proceeding` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 24 the General Division may call for and examine the record of the civil proceedings` `District Court` FALSE `a criminal proceeding` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 24 the General Division may call for and examine the record of the civil proceedings` `Court of Appeal` FALSE `a civil proceeding` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 24 the General Division may call for and examine the record of the civil proceedings` `another subordinate court, tribunal or judicial or quasi-judicial body` TRUE `a civil proceeding` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 25: inputs are the court, the appeal-right flag, the nature, the record called for or otherwise known, the orders seem necessary
#ASSERT (`s 25 the General Division may give such orders on the civil proceedings, including directing a new trial` `District Court` FALSE `a civil proceeding` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 25 the General Division may give such orders on the civil proceedings, including directing a new trial` `District Court` FALSE `a civil proceeding` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 25 the General Division may give such orders on the civil proceedings, including directing a new trial` `District Court` FALSE `a civil proceeding` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 25 the General Division may give such orders on the civil proceedings, including directing a new trial` `District Court` FALSE `a criminal proceeding` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 25 the General Division may give such orders on the civil proceedings, including directing a new trial` `Court of Appeal` FALSE `a civil proceeding` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 26: no revision at the instance of a party who could have appealed`

-- the twin: inputs are an appeal lies, no appeal is brought
#ASSERT (`s 26 the section applies to the civil matter` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 26 the section applies to the civil matter` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 26 the section applies to the civil matter` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- inputs: an appeal lies, no appeal is brought, the party could have appealed
#ASSERT (`s 26 a proceeding by way of revision may be entertained at the instance of the party` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the party could not have appealed: s 26 grants nothing
#ASSERT (`s 26 a proceeding by way of revision may be entertained at the instance of the party` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- an appeal was brought: s 26 does not apply
#ASSERT (`s 26 a proceeding by way of revision may be entertained at the instance of the party` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- no appeal lies: s 26 does not apply
#ASSERT (`s 26 a proceeding by way of revision may be entertained at the instance of the party` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 27: general supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction`

#ASSERT (`s 27(1) the General Division has general supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction over the court` `District Court` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 27(1) the General Division has general supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction over the court` `Magistrate's Court` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 27(1) the General Division has general supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction over the court` `Syariah Court` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 27(1) the General Division has general supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction over the court` `Syariah Court` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 27(1) the General Division has general supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction over the court` `Court of Appeal` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): inputs are the step, the court, the appeal-right flag, desirable in the interests of justice
#ASSERT (`s 27(2) the General Division may take the step in the matter or proceeding` `s 27(2) calls for the record` `District Court` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 27(2) the General Division may take the step in the matter or proceeding` `s 27(2) removes the matter or proceeding into the General Division` `Magistrate's Court` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 27(2) the General Division may take the step in the matter or proceeding` `s 27(2) gives the subordinate court directions as to the further conduct of the matter or proceeding` `Family Court` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "if it appears desirable in the interests of justice": not met
#ASSERT (`s 27(2) the General Division may take the step in the matter or proceeding` `s 27(2) calls for the record` `District Court` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a subordinate court
#ASSERT (`s 27(2) the General Division may take the step in the matter or proceeding` `s 27(2) calls for the record` `Court of Appeal` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): inputs are the record called for under (2), a further order made
#ASSERT (`s 27(3) the proceedings in the subordinate court are stayed` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 27(3) the proceedings in the subordinate court are stayed` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 27(3) the proceedings in the subordinate court are stayed` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 27(3) the proceedings in the subordinate court are stayed` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4): inputs are exercising or deciding whether to exercise, the matter concerns a case of an appeal from a subordinate court
#ASSERT (`s 27(4) the General Division is to have regard to whether the matter was or could reasonably have been raised in the appeal` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 27(4) the General Division is to have regard to whether the matter was or could reasonably have been raised in the appeal` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 27(4) the General Division is to have regard to whether the matter was or could reasonably have been raised in the appeal` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The regulative rule for (4), run: a General Division that has regard is FULFILLED; one that decides without having that regard leaves the duty standing (the section sets no time);
-- where (4) does not apply the rule is FULFILLED at once. (Read from the output of `l4 run`: FULFILLED, a residual MUST, FULFILLED.)
#TRACE `s 27(4) the General Division must have regard to whether the matter was or could reasonably have been raised in the appeal` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 27(4) the General Division` DOES `s 27(4) has regard to whether the matter was or could reasonably have been raised in the appeal` AT 1
#TRACE `s 27(4) the General Division must have regard to whether the matter was or could reasonably have been raised in the appeal` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 27(4) the General Division` DOES `s 27(4) decides without having that regard` AT 1
#TRACE `s 27(4) the General Division must have regard to whether the matter was or could reasonably have been raised in the appeal` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 27(4) the General Division` DOES `s 27(4) decides without having that regard` AT 1

§§ `s 28: discretion of the General Division as to hearing parties`

-- (1): inputs are exercising powers of supervision and revision, a written law gives the right
#ASSERT (`s 28(1) the party has a right to be heard before the General Division` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 28(1) the party has a right to be heard before the General Division` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 28(1) the party has a right to be heard before the General Division` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): inputs are a final order made to the prejudice of the person, the person has had an opportunity of being heard
#ASSERT (`s 28(2) the final order may be made to the prejudice of the person` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 28(2) the final order may be made to the prejudice of the person` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 28(2) the final order may be made to the prejudice of the person` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the twin for the bar: applies where a final order is made to the person's prejudice and they have not been heard; once the "unless" is met it does not
#ASSERT (`s 28(2) the bar on a final order made to the prejudice of the person applies` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 28(2) the bar on a final order made to the prejudice of the person applies` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 28(2) the bar on a final order made to the prejudice of the person applies` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 28(2) the bar on a final order made to the prejudice of the person applies` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 28A: allocation of proceedings to the District Court or Family Court`

-- (1): inputs are the Chief Justice considers it necessary or expedient, the direction is by order
#ASSERT (`s 28A(1) the Chief Justice may by order direct the class of proceedings to be heard and determined by the District Court or Family Court` TRUE TRUE `District Court`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 28A(1) the Chief Justice may by order direct the class of proceedings to be heard and determined by the District Court or Family Court` TRUE TRUE `Family Court`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a direction to a court the subsection does not name (no "only"): not decided
#ASSERT (`s 28A(1) the Chief Justice may by order direct the class of proceedings to be heard and determined by the District Court or Family Court` TRUE TRUE `Magistrate's Court`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 28A(1) the Chief Justice may by order direct the class of proceedings to be heard and determined by the District Court or Family Court` FALSE TRUE `Magistrate's Court`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 28A(1) the Chief Justice may by order direct the class of proceedings to be heard and determined by the District Court or Family Court` FALSE TRUE `District Court`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 28A(1) the Chief Justice may by order direct the class of proceedings to be heard and determined by the District Court or Family Court` TRUE FALSE `District Court`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): inputs are the provision, the order is made under (1), the subject, the District Court would lack jurisdiction only because of the amount
#ASSERT (`s 28A(2) an order under section 28A(1) may make the provision` `s 28A(2)(a)(i) confer jurisdiction on a District Court over proceedings it would lack only because the amount exceeds its monetary limit` TRUE `any other civil matter` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a)(i) is for proceedings the District Court lacks only by reason of the amount
#ASSERT (`s 28A(2) an order under section 28A(1) may make the provision` `s 28A(2)(a)(i) confer jurisdiction on a District Court over proceedings it would lack only because the amount exceeds its monetary limit` TRUE `any other civil matter` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a)(ii): the matters in s 17(1)(b) or (c): admiralty or shipping, bankruptcy, companies
#ASSERT (`s 28A(2) an order under section 28A(1) may make the provision` `s 28A(2)(a)(ii) confer jurisdiction on a District Court over proceedings relating to a matter in section 17(1)(b) or (c)` TRUE `admiralty or shipping` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 28A(2) an order under section 28A(1) may make the provision` `s 28A(2)(a)(ii) confer jurisdiction on a District Court over proceedings relating to a matter in section 17(1)(b) or (c)` TRUE bankruptcy FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 28A(2) an order under section 28A(1) may make the provision` `s 28A(2)(a)(ii) confer jurisdiction on a District Court over proceedings relating to a matter in section 17(1)(b) or (c)` TRUE companies FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a matter in s 17(1)(a) (divorce) is not one of them
#ASSERT (`s 28A(2) an order under section 28A(1) may make the provision` `s 28A(2)(a)(ii) confer jurisdiction on a District Court over proceedings relating to a matter in section 17(1)(b) or (c)` TRUE `divorce and matrimonial causes` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 28A(2) an order under section 28A(1) may make the provision` `s 28A(2)(aa) confer jurisdiction on a Family Court over proceedings it would not otherwise have jurisdiction to hear and determine` TRUE `any other civil matter` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 28A(2) an order under section 28A(1) may make the provision` `s 28A(2)(b) make provision governing appeals relating to proceedings transferred, including restricting the right of appeal` TRUE `any other civil matter` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 28A(2) an order under section 28A(1) may make the provision` `s 28A(2)(c) make incidental provision for the transfer of the proceedings, including procedure and costs` TRUE `any other civil matter` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an order not made under (1)
#ASSERT (`s 28A(2) an order under section 28A(1) may make the provision` `s 28A(2)(c) make incidental provision for the transfer of the proceedings, including procedure and costs` FALSE `any other civil matter` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
